{"step_index":165,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:49:11Z","thinking":"**Adding Favicon Assets**\n\nI'm now integrating the `ensure_favicon_assets()` function into `app.py`. This involves checking for the logo image file and generating the necessary favicon assets, ensuring the `.ico` file exists in the public directory and the `.png` is in images. The goal is to make sure these files exist, creating them from the logo if needed, before the application runs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>StreamWave Entertainment | Serverless Media Platform</title>\n    \n    <!-- Favicon Links for Browser Tab Logo Icon -->\n    <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/png\" href=\"/images/favicon.png\">\n    <link rel=\"shortcut icon\" type=\"image/x-icon\" href=\"/favicon.ico\">\n    <link rel=\"apple-touch-icon\" href=\"/images/favicon.png\">\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/css/styles.css\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n</head>\n<body>\n    <!-- Navigation Bar -->\n    <header class=\"navbar\">\n        <div class=\"nav-container\">\n            <a href=\"#featured\" class=\"brand\" aria-label=\"StreamWave Entertainment Home\">\n                <img src=\"/images/streamwave-logo.png\" alt=\"StreamWave Entertainment Logo\" class=\"brand-logo-img\">\n            </a>\n\n            <nav class=\"nav-links\" aria-label=\"Primary Navigation\">\n                <a href=\"#featured\" class=\"nav-link active\">Home</a>\n                <a href=\"#catalogue\" class=\"nav-link\">Catalogue</a>\n     